**How to implement.** Correcting an experiment's setup after the fact, with a mandatory audit note, as a semantic message (001 §P `CorrectSetup`; 001 §K 'Corrections: re-point an experiment's setup after the fact (e.g. "LR was at −45"), with a mandatory audit note'; the S9.3 brief: the lab file is untouched; the S9.1 mapper's request: CorrectSetup re-points `Experiment.setup`, an edit keeping the name). The view that sends it is step 326's. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`, beside `withRole` (step 294): `type Experiment with member this.correctedTo (setup : SetupReference) (note : CorrectionNote) : Experiment`, the experiment over `setup` whose `corrections` end with `{ previous = this.setup; corrected = setup; note }` (step 313); its name, scan, role, session, notes and data are unchanged, so a lab file keyed by its name still matches it. Pinning follows: the corrected setup's revision is pinned by `Setup.pinFor` (step 261) because the experiment now references it. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `SetCorrectionNote of ControlCaption` sets `dataDraft.correctionNote` (step 315), writing nothing; `CorrectSetup of Experiments.ExperimentId * SetupReference * ControlCaption` (re-point the experiment to that setup revision, for that note), each with a one-line doc, refused by the read-only guard of step 185. Its arm: an experiment the collection lacks changes nothing; a note `CorrectionNote.tryCreate` refuses sets `kitStatus` to `Not corrected — a correction needs an audit note.`; a reference no setup of `model.kitSetups` answers at its revision (`slotsAt`, step 256) `Not corrected — the kit holds no setup <reference.describe>.`; the experiment's own reference `Not corrected — <name> already references <reference.describe>.`; each writes nothing. Otherwise `experiment.correctedTo reference note` is recorded through `KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment` (step 261): on `Ok` the collection takes it (`withStoredExperiment`), its badge is computed again by the one private validation function (the detector may differ in the corrected slots), `reviewedDataOpt` is read again when it reviews this experiment, and `kitStatus` is `Corrected <name>: <previous.describe> → <reference.describe> (<note>).`; on `Error e` the model is kept with `kitStatus` `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. Nothing reads or writes the lab file, and the experiment keeps its name and its file. No other message, field or option is added. Tests. `ExperimentProxyTests` gains `a correction re-points the experiment's setup and appends the audit entry, its name and data unchanged`: a test-local experiment named `CPL-(LR#45)-CPL` over `CPL-(LR#45)-CPL` revision 1 with a mapped attachment, `correctedTo` `CPL-(LR#-45)-CPL` revision 1 with the note `LR was at -45` is over that reference, its corrections holding exactly that entry, and its name, scan, role and data equal to before; a second correction back appends a second entry after it. `ExperimentModelTests` (step 292), over its folder kit with `E1` committed over `Setup 1` and the polarizer then turned to R1 30° and recorded by `CreateSetup` as `Bench B` (step 260), E1's data attached as step 315 attaches it: `CorrectSetup re-points the experiment to a setup of the kit with its audit note, and the lab file and the experiment's name are untouched`: `CorrectSetup (ExperimentId 1, <Bench B revision 1>, ControlCaption "LP1 was at 30")` leaves E1 over `Bench B` revision 1 with one correction from `Setup 1` revision 1 and that note, `E1.experiment-json` read back holding the same, the name `E1`, the attached file's bytes unchanged and `kitStatus` `Corrected E1: 'Setup 1' revision 1 → 'Bench B' revision 1 (LP1 was at 30).`. `a correction without a note, to a setup the kit lacks, or to the setup it already references writes nothing`: `CorrectSetup` with the note `"  "`, to `Gone` revision 1, and to `Setup 1` revision 1 while E1 is over it each set the `kitStatus` above and leave every file's bytes unchanged. `KitWindowModelTests`: `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` also sends `CorrectSetup`, with its assertions.

**Acceptance.** After `CorrectSetup` lands, it MUST re-point an experiment to a setup revision the kit holds and append the audit entry (previous, corrected, non-blank note) to its file, its name, scan and data unchanged and the lab file untouched, refused typed for a blank note, an unknown or unchanged setup and a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a correction re-points the experiment's setup and appends the audit entry, its name and data unchanged`, `CorrectSetup re-points the experiment to a setup of the kit with its audit note, and the lab file and the experiment's name are untouched` and `a correction without a note, to a setup the kit lacks, or to the setup it already references writes nothing`, the count rising by 3, and the changed `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.
